Jahshaka patch 0087: the EMISSIVE voxel store is an RGBA16F float, so an emitter
authored above 1.0 reaches the light injection intact. (PHOTON phase A,
VOXEL-CLIP-1, 2026-09-22. SOURCE + MEDIA: every tree resets the submodule and
re-runs build-ogre.sh.)

WHAT IT CHANGES
  * VctVoxelizer::createVoxelTextures: mEmissiveVox is PFG_RGBA16_FLOAT instead
    of PFG_RGBA8_UNORM. That is the whole functional change -- ONE line.
  * Voxelizer_piece_cs.any: a COMMENT ONLY, in the D3D11-without-typed-UAV-loads
    branch, saying why that branch keeps packing UNORM8 and what a D3D11 port has
    to fix. No code in any shader moves.

WHY (SPECS/photon/A2_VOXEL_CLIP_DESIGN.md)
  Albedo is a ratio and lives in [0, 1] by definition. EMISSIVE is a radiance --
  W/(m^2 sr) -- and a lamp, a screen or a sky panel is authored above 1.0 as a
  matter of course. Every other stage of this engine already carried it honestly:
  VctMaterial stores four floats per datablock (shaderMaterial.emissive[i] =
  emissiveCol[i]), our order-independent merge accumulates it on a fixed-point
  grid whose per-contribution clamp is 16.0 (patch 0065), and the lit volume has
  been a float since patch 0080. The one clip left was the final store, and it
  was total: an emitter at radiance 3.0 was written as exactly 1.0, and
  LightInjection seeds the radiance volume straight off that texel
  (blockColour = emissiveVal.xyz), so a third of the emitter's energy entered the
  bounces, the irradiance field, the diffuse cones and the ray hits -- with no
  hitch, no log line, and a picture that merely looks dimmer. Measured before this
  patch on tests/rtreflect's lamp arm: a PERFECT MIRROR showing an emitter of
  radiance 3.0 read 0.333x of it, i.e. exactly 1.0, when radiance is invariant
  along a ray and it must read 3.0.

  RGBA16_FLOAT and not 32: half carries 65504 with an 11-bit mantissa, finer than
  the merge's own 1/4096 grid everywhere in [0, 16]. So the HEADROOM RULE is now
  stated by ONE constant: VOXEL_MERGE_CLAMP (16.0) in Voxelizer_piece_cs.any is
  the documented ceiling per contribution, beyond which the merge saturates. There
  is no silent clip at 1.0 anywhere in the chain.

WHY NOTHING ELSE MOVES (verified at this pin, and it is worth writing down)
  * The GLSL image declaration carries NO hard-coded format qualifier:
    Voxelizer_cs.glsl declares voxelEmissiveTex through an inserted piece that
    HlmsComputeJob generates from the BOUND TEXTURE's pixel format
    (OgreHlmsComputeJob.cpp setProperties: uav4_pf_type ->
    VulkanPixelFormatToShaderType::getPixelFormatType -> "rgba16f"). The
    commented-out layout lines further down that file naming rgba8 are upstream's
    own dead notes and are deliberately left alone.
  * The typed-UAV write is a float4 in both cases (OGRE_imageWrite3D4 of
    voxelMergeEmissive's result), so no shader text changes.
  * ComputeTools::clearUavFloat asserts only that the format is NOT INTEGER and
    dispatches Compute/Tools/ClearUav, which declares its UAV from the same
    generated pieces -- a float 3D clear of any non-integer format. (Unlike patch
    0065's MergeAccum note: it is a 128-bit clear that loses the device on this
    driver, not a float one. 64 bits clears correctly; measured.)
  * Every READER loads it as a sampled texture (LightInjection_cs.glsl:
    uniform texture3D voxelEmissiveTex, read by texelFetch), which returns floats
    whatever the store.
  * VoxelizedMeshCache's cached copies take the format through
    copyParametersFrom(voxelizer.getEmissiveVox()).

COST (Showroom 2 at High, this rig, Xvfb 1920x1080, one chain of four cascades)
  VRAM: the emissive volumes go from 18.00 MB to 36.00 MB (2 x 128^3 at 8 -> 16 MB
  and 2 x 64^3 at 1 -> 2 MB); the whole VCT texture set 365 MB -> 383 MB.
  A cascade rebuild (voxelise + the first light injection: the gi/vct.cascadeN
  cache-work row of a perf.capture, eight rebuilds of the chain per run, forced by
  a camera teleport away and back): CPU 2.05 ms mean before, 1.63 ms after, and a
  SECOND patched run read 1.33 ms -- so the change is BELOW this instrument's
  run-to-run spread and no cost increase is measurable. The GPU halves move the
  same way (6.5 / 4.2 / 3.6 ms), as do rows this patch cannot touch
  (gi/ifd.converge 3.02 / 1.92 ms), which is what says it is the environment:
  the clocks are not locked under Xvfb and each arm is a different process.
  Mechanically there is no reason to expect one -- the write is one imageStore per
  covered voxel and the dispatch is bound by the triangle walk.

diff --git a/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.cpp b/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.cpp
index 96f1c3834..6d4bc9612 100644
--- a/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.cpp
+++ b/Components/Hlms/Pbs/src/Vct/OgreVctVoxelizer.cpp
@@ -907,7 +907,34 @@ namespace Ogre
             textures[i]->scheduleTransitionTo( GpuResidency::OnStorage );
 
         mAlbedoVox->setPixelFormat( PFG_RGBA8_UNORM );
-        mEmissiveVox->setPixelFormat( PFG_RGBA8_UNORM );
+        // JAHSHAKA PATCH 0087: THE EMISSIVE VOXEL IS A FLOAT.
+        //
+        // Albedo is a RATIO and lives in [0, 1] by definition, so its UNORM store
+        // above is exact. EMISSIVE is a RADIANCE -- W/(m^2 sr), no upper bound
+        // worth naming -- and this store was the one place it was clipped: the
+        // material store carries it as four honest floats (VctMaterial:
+        // shaderMaterial.emissive[i] = emissiveCol[i]) and the merge accumulates
+        // it on a fixed-point grid clamped at 16.0 per contribution (patch 0065),
+        // but the final imageWrite went into a UNORM8 texel, so an emitter
+        // authored at 3.0 was stored as exactly 1.0 and the light injection seeded
+        // the radiance volume from that (LightInjection_piece_cs.any:
+        // blockColour = emissiveVal.xyz) -- a third of the energy, entering the
+        // bounces, the irradiance field, the cones and the ray hits, with nothing
+        // in any log and a picture that merely looks dimmer.
+        //
+        // RGBA16_FLOAT and not 32: half carries 65504 with 11 bits of mantissa,
+        // which is finer than the merge's own 1/4096 grid everywhere in [0, 16] --
+        // the grid's clamp, not the format, is now the documented ceiling.
+        //
+        // NOTHING ELSE MOVES. The GLSL image declaration carries no hard-coded
+        // format: HlmsComputeJob generates the layout qualifier from the bound
+        // texture (uav4_pf_type, OgreHlmsComputeJob.cpp), the typed-UAV write is a
+        // float4 either way, ComputeTools::clearUavFloat clears any non-integer
+        // format, and every reader loads through a sampled texture3D. The one
+        // backend that cannot follow is D3D11 WITHOUT typed UAV loads, whose
+        // branch packs the texel into a single uint -- see the note beside it in
+        // Voxelizer_piece_cs.any.
+        mEmissiveVox->setPixelFormat( PFG_RGBA16_FLOAT );
         mNormalVox->setPixelFormat( PFG_R10G10B10A2_UNORM );
         if( hasTypedUavs )
             mAccumValVox->setPixelFormat( PFG_R16_UINT );
diff --git a/Samples/Media/VCT/Voxelizer_piece_cs.any b/Samples/Media/VCT/Voxelizer_piece_cs.any
index 09d049a06..8f0d572d0 100644
--- a/Samples/Media/VCT/Voxelizer_piece_cs.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/VCT/Voxelizer_piece_cs.any
@@ -539,6 +539,18 @@
 			OGRE_imageWrite3D4( voxelEmissiveTex, voxelCelUvw, voxelEmissive );
 			OGRE_imageWrite3D1( voxelAccumVal, voxelCelUvw, uint4( totalTris, 0, 0, 0 ) );
 		@else
+			// JAHSHAKA PATCH 0087: THE BRANCH THAT CANNOT FOLLOW THE FLOAT STORE.
+			// This is D3D11 without typed UAV loads, where each texel is packed
+			// into ONE 32-bit uint, and the emissive volume is now RGBA16_FLOAT
+			// (64 bits per texel, OgreVctVoxelizer.cpp createVoxelTextures): a
+			// half pair per channel needs two uints, so this path would need the
+			// volume declared as a two-component uint image to carry it. It is
+			// left packing UNORM8 deliberately -- this tree ships Vulkan only,
+			// the GLSL and Metal paths take the branch above, and a silent
+			// half-written texel would be worse than a documented ceiling. A
+			// D3D11 port fixes this line together with the image declaration in
+			// Voxelizer_cs.hlsl; the emissive clip at 1.0 is what it inherits
+			// until then.
 			OGRE_imageWrite3D4( voxelAlbedoTex, voxelCelUvw, packUnorm4x8( voxelAlbedo ) );
 			OGRE_imageWrite3D4( voxelNormalTex, voxelCelUvw, packUnormRGB10A2( voxelNormal ) );
 			OGRE_imageWrite3D4( voxelEmissiveTex, voxelCelUvw, packUnorm4x8( voxelEmissive ) );
